🧠 Introduction

LangChain is one of the most popular frameworks for building:

✔ RAG systems
✔ AI agents
✔ Chatbots
✔ LLM applications

Core building blocks include:

* Documents
* Loaders
* Retrievers

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📄 1. Documents

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is a Document?

```text id="document_def"
A structured object containing text content and metadata
```

---

🧾 Structure of a Document

A document usually contains:

* `page_content`
* `metadata`

---

💻 Example

```python id="document_example"
from langchain.schema import Document

doc = Document(
    page_content="Artificial Intelligence is transforming industries.",
    metadata={"source": "ai_article.pdf"}
)

print(doc.page_content)
print(doc.metadata)
```

---

🎯 Why Documents Matter

✔ Standardized format
✔ Easy processing
✔ Supports metadata filtering
✔ Used throughout RAG pipelines

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📂 2. Document Loaders

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is a Loader?

```text id="loader_def2"
A component that reads data from files, websites, or databases
```

---

🔹 Popular Loaders

| Loader        | Purpose         |
| ------------- | --------------- |
| PyPDFLoader   | Load PDFs       |
| CSVLoader     | Load CSV files  |
| WebBaseLoader | Load web pages  |
| TextLoader    | Load text files |

---

💻 Example: PDF Loader

```python id="pdf_loader_example2"
from langchain.document_loaders import PyPDFLoader

loader = PyPDFLoader("report.pdf")
documents = loader.load()

print(documents[0].page_content)
```

---

💻 Example: URL Loader

```python id="url_loader_example2"
from langchain.document_loaders import WebBaseLoader

loader = WebBaseLoader("https://example.com")
documents = loader.load()
```

---

🔧 Benefits of Loaders

✔ Handle multiple file types
✔ Preserve metadata
✔ Simplify ingestion pipelines

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔍 3. Retrievers

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is a Retriever?

```text id="retriever_def2"
A component that fetches the most relevant documents for a query
```

---

🎯 Retriever Workflow

```text id="retriever_flow"
User Query → Query Embedding → Similarity Search → Relevant Documents
```

---

🔹 Why Retrievers are Important

✔ Improve answer relevance
✔ Reduce hallucinations
✔ Enable scalable search

---

💻 Example: Create Retriever

```python id="retriever_example"
retriever = vector_store.as_retriever(
    search_kwargs={"k": 4}
)
```

---

📌 Query Example

```python id="retriever_query"
docs = retriever.get_relevant_documents(
    "Explain machine learning"
)

print(docs[0].page_content)
```

---

🔍 Types of Retrievers

| Retriever                        | Purpose                    |
| -------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Similarity Retriever             | Basic semantic search      |
| MMR Retriever                    | Diversity-aware retrieval  |
| MultiQuery Retriever             | Multiple query variations  |
| Contextual Compression Retriever | Compress retrieved content |

---

🧠 MMR Retriever

MMR = Maximum Marginal Relevance

Balances:

✔ Relevance
✔ Diversity

---

📘 Example

Instead of retrieving very similar chunks:

* Retrieve diverse but relevant chunks.

---

🔄 Complete LangChain Flow

```text id="langchain_flow"
Loader → Documents → Splitter → Embeddings → Vector Store → Retriever → LLM
```

---

🚀 Real-World Applications

✔ PDF Chatbots
✔ Enterprise Search
✔ Legal Document QA
✔ Research Assistants
✔ Customer Support Bots

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔧 Best Practices

✔ Preserve metadata
✔ Use recursive chunking
✔ Tune retriever `k` value
✔ Combine retrievers with reranking

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Large irrelevant chunks
❌ No metadata
❌ Poor retriever settings
❌ Over-fetching documents

---

🧠 Interview Answer (Simple)

> In LangChain, documents store text and metadata, loaders ingest data from different sources, and retrievers fetch the most relevant chunks for a user query in RAG systems.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Documents are structured text objects
✔ Loaders ingest data from multiple sources
✔ Retrievers find relevant chunks using embeddings
✔ Core building blocks of RAG applications

